Radxa RK3576 FAT boot logo
===========================

The ROCK 4D, ROCK 4D SPI and NX4 C200 configurations can load a replaceable
BMP logo from FAT without embedding the image in u-boot.itb. The feature is
enabled by CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_FAT_LOGO and runs when the extlinux boot method
finds a valid bootflow on a block device.

Deployment
----------

Copy one or two uncompressed BMP files to the root of a FAT partition on the
same block device as the extlinux bootflow:

  sudo cp logo.bmp /path/to/fat/logo.bmp
  sudo cp logo_kernel.bmp /path/to/fat/logo_kernel.bmp
  sync

The FAT partition does not have to contain extlinux.conf. U-Boot checks FAT
partitions in partition-number order and uses the first /logo.bmp it finds.
For example, Linux may mount the selected FAT partition at /config or
/boot/efi, while extlinux.conf and the root filesystem reside on ext4.
The Linux mount path is not part of the U-Boot filename.

Replacing either BMP changes it without rebuilding U-Boot. As in the existing
distro FAT-logo flow, a missing /logo.bmp is simply skipped and does not
prevent OS boot. logo_kernel.bmp is optional; when missing, Linux handoff
reuses logo.bmp. Empty, oversized or invalid BMP files are also ignored. The
maximum input file size is 16 MiB per image. Use 24-bit, uncompressed BMPs
whose dimensions fit the display and the DRM logo memory.

Loading and handoff
-------------------

After a block-device extlinux bootflow becomes ready, U-Boot scans that
device's FAT partitions, reads /logo.bmp, validates its BMP header and declared
size, decodes it into the Rockchip DRM logo buffer and displays it. If
/logo_kernel.bmp exists on the same partition, U-Boot decodes it into a second
cache entry without displaying it yet.

During rockchip_display_fixup(), U-Boot selects the cached logo_kernel.bmp for
Rockchip DRM loader-logo handoff. If unavailable, it reuses the decoded
logo.bmp cache. It passes the selected image's reserved-memory address, offset,
dimensions, format and display timing to a compatible Rockchip Linux DRM
driver.

Scope and limitations
---------------------

- The feature applies to block-device extlinux bootflows, not PXE/network boot.
- U-Boot must reach the extlinux scan before the image can appear. On an empty
  disk containing only SPL/U-Boot, no FAT logo is available.
- The image is not authenticated by the U-Boot FIT hash/signature. Protect the
  FAT filesystem separately if untrusted logo replacement matters.
- No new environment-variable switch is added; this follows the existing
  file-presence behavior.
- Updating only U-Boot does not replace the FAT image. Repartitioning or
  formatting the selected FAT partition does.
- The first automatic board_late_init resource-logo attempt may print a
  harmless failure before extlinux identifies the FAT device. FAT loading is
  performed later by bootmeth_extlinux.

Validation
----------

U-Boot should print, for example:

  Loading boot logo from partition 1:/logo.bmp
  Caching kernel logo from partition 1:/logo_kernel.bmp

Linux should expose a non-zero /reserved-memory/drm-logo region and logo
offset/width/height/bpp properties on the active display route. These checks
confirm the data and handoff path; use a display capture when flicker-free
visual continuity is a release requirement.
